<section class="mh-about-origin reveal" id="origin">
  <div class="mh-about-inner">
    <div class="mh-eyebrow">The Origin</div>
    <h2 class="mh-about-origin-headline">Born from 25+ Years of Global Enterprise Leadership</h2>

    <div class="mh-about-origin-body">
      <p>Most platforms start with a feature idea. MedhaIQ started with a pattern noticed over two and a half decades.</p>
      <p>Across twenty-five years leading global consulting practices, enterprise transformations, and talent initiatives spanning North America, EMEA, and APAC, one thing held true across every industry and every level: technical skill opens the door, but the ability to structure an argument, read a room, and communicate under pressure decides how far someone walks through it.</p>
      <p>Sitting across the table in board reviews, client pitches, and executive interviews, the people who made the strongest impression were rarely the ones who knew the most. They were the ones who could take something complex and make it clear, make a judgment call and defend it, and stay composed when the questions got hard.</p>
      <p>And yet the way most professionals prepare for these moments hasn't caught up:</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="mh-about-gaps">
      <li class="mh-about-gap">
        <span class="mh-about-gap-mark">01</span>
        <span class="mh-about-gap-text"><strong>Feedback arrives too late to matter.</strong> A rejection email or a once-a-year review is a verdict, delivered after the moment has already passed.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="mh-about-gap">
        <span class="mh-about-gap-mark">02</span>
        <span class="mh-about-gap-text"><strong>The first real attempt happens at the highest stakes.</strong> Professionals are expected to perform flawlessly without ever practicing in a setting rigorous enough to prepare them.</span>
      </li>
      <li class="mh-about-gap">
        <span class="mh-about-gap-mark">03</span>
        <span class="mh-about-gap-text"><strong>Evaluation is a matter of opinion, not evidence.</strong> Careers turn on subjective impressions rather than anything a person can actually see, measure, or act on.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mh-about-origin-close">MedhaIQ exists to close that gap — pairing enterprise-grade evaluation standards with adaptive AI, so professionals can practice honestly, get evaluated rigorously, and walk into the real moment already having done the hard part once before.</p>

